      "Language": "ita",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The case of a 64 year-old man suffering from angina caused by neoplastic infiltration of the left anterior descending coronary artery is reported. The coronarographic examination of the vessel disclosed that it had a stenotic segment, which did not move with the cardiac contraction. An aorto-coronary by-pass vein graft relieved the symptoms."},
